  "readmeFile": "ReadMe.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### 7.0.286\nFix: The managed AMS/TCP router now rejects AMS/TCP frames whose declared body size (TcpHeader.cbSize) exceeds 64 MiB before allocating the receive buffer, and closes the connection. This prevents a memory-exhaustion denial-of-service where a crafted 6-byte header forced an arbitrarily large allocation.\n### 7.0.60\nEnh: AmsRouter not using app local UnixSocket path as fallback anymore.\nEnh: Using LoopbackConnection as fallback, when no UnixSocket path is specified by configuration.\n### 7.0.36\nBreaking Change: Removes .NET6 as Dependency (out-of-support)\n### 7.0\nEnh: Supports internal communication via UnixSockets or TCP/IP Loopback\nEnh: TargetFramework dependencies changed to net8.0, net6.0, netstandard2.0",
